.\" karvi-prune(8): the retention helper's manual page. Written by hand
.\" except the two generated regions, which tools/mangen rewrites from the
.\" helper's flag definition (make generate); docs/PRUNE.md is the guide and
.\" states the same rules, the report, and the exits, so a change to the
.\" helper changes both.
.TH KARVI-PRUNE 8 "" "karvi"
.\" Paths and options are not hyphenated, and lines are not stretched.
.nh
.ds AD l
.ad l
.SH NAME
karvi\-prune \- remove finished karvi work older than the retention age
.SH SYNOPSIS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED SYNOPSIS: tools/mangen from internal/prune; edit there
.B karvi\-prune
.RB [ "\-\-basedir \fIauto|PATH\fP" ]
.RB [ "\-\-sharedroot \fIauto|none|PATH\fP" ]
.RB [ "\-\-scoreboards \fIPATH\fP" ]
.RB [ "\-\-days \fIN\fP" ]
.RB [ "\-\-minfree \fIPERCENT\fP" ]
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose ]
.RB [ "\-\-format \fItext|jsonl\fP" ]
.\" END GENERATED SYNOPSIS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B karvi\-prune
removes finished work older than the retention age from the trees karvi
writes, and leaves everything else where it is: the job folders of
finished jobs, recorded login transcripts, final scoreboard files, the
folders a job left without its summary, the scoreboard files a crashed
daemon left at a running status, and the day folders those leave empty.
The per-operator timer, the site's root timer, the cron script, and a
hand run all invoke it with the same flags, so they make the same
decisions.
.PP
It never removes a running job, a transcript still being recorded, a
folder whose name is not a
.I YYMMDD
day folder, a symbolic link, a file it cannot read, the collection
directory of
.BR "karvi crun" ,
the audit log, or anything in journald.
.PP
It reads no configuration: its flags carry the settings' words
.RB ( auto ,
.BR none ,
a path), and a timer's or cron line holds a site's values.
.B HOME
does not move the private root; the home is the password database's.
.PP
A run removes what its user owns, wherever it is, and passes every other
user's item by, counted as
.BR not_owned ;
a run as root removes everything eligible.
In a shared tree a job folder is mode 2750 in its operator's name, so a
colleague can read it and cannot empty it, while root can.
.PP
A removal that fails is reported as a
.B failed
line with its reason and the run goes on to the next item; the summary
counts it and the exit is 1.
.SH OPTIONS
.\" BEGIN GENERATED OPTIONS: tools/mangen from internal/prune; edit there
.TP
.BI \-\-basedir " auto|PATH"
The private root whose jobs and transcripts trees are pruned: auto (the operator's own, as karvi resolves it) or a path.
Default: \fBauto\fP.
.TP
.BI \-\-sharedroot " auto|none|PATH"
The site's shared root whose jobs and transcripts trees are pruned too: auto, none, or a path.
Default: \fBauto\fP.
.TP
.BI \-\-scoreboards " PATH"
The scoreboard directory (watch.directory).
Default: \fB/dev/shm/karvi/scoreboards\fP.
.TP
.BI \-\-days " N"
The retention age in days, one or more.
Default: \fB31\fP.
.TP
.BI \-\-minfree " PERCENT"
The free\-space floor in percent, under which the oldest eligible items go before their age; 0 turns pressure off.
Default: \fB5\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report what would go and remove nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Add one kept line per examined item that stays, with the reason.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " text|jsonl"
The report's form: text (an event word and key=value fields per line) or jsonl (one JSON document per line, the same fields, the summary last).
Default: \fBtext\fP.
.\" END GENERATED OPTIONS
.SH WHAT GOES
Each kind is judged against the retention age,
.BR \-\-days ;
the cutoff is now less that many days.
.TP
.B activity
A job folder whose
.I summary.json
has a final status
.RB ( completed ,
.BR halted ,
.BR errored ,
.BR cancelled ,
.BR incomplete ,
or
.BR exercised ).
Goes when its
.I ended_at
is before the cutoff; pressure takes it, oldest first.
.TP
.B transcript
A recorded login: the metadata file with its end record and the
transcript that shares its name.
Goes when its
.I ended_at
is before the cutoff; pressure takes it.
.TP
.B scoreboard
A scoreboard file at a final status.
Goes when its
.I last_updated_at
is before the cutoff; pressure takes it.
.TP
.B orphan
A job folder without
.IR summary.json :
a job the daemon's death cut short, or one run with
.B output.files.summary\-json
false.
Goes when its day folder's date is before the cutoff, nothing in it is
newer, and its scoreboard file, if any, is final or older than the age;
pressure never takes it.
.TP
.B stale\-scoreboard
A scoreboard file at a running status that nothing has touched for the
age, the file a crashed daemon's job leaves.
Goes when its
.I last_updated_at
is before the cutoff; pressure never takes it.
.TP
.B day
A
.I YYMMDD
day folder that holds nothing.
Goes when its date is before the cutoff, after the run's other removals,
with a plain
.BR rmdir ,
so a folder that gained a job in the meantime stays; pressure never
takes it.
.PP
.B Pressure.
.B \-\-minfree
is a free-space floor in percent.
A tree whose filesystem is under the floor gives up its oldest finished
items
.RB ( activity ,
.BR transcript ,
.BR scoreboard )
before their age, one at a time until the floor is met, the newest kept.
The floor is judged on each tree's own filesystem.
.B "\-\-minfree 0"
turns pressure off.
.SH WHERE IT LOOKS
As an operator, with nothing given:
.IP 1. 4
The private root,
.BR "\-\-basedir auto" ,
the first that exists of
.IR /opt/karvi/users/USER ,
.IR /var/lib/karvi/users/USER ,
and
.IR \(ti/.local/share/karvi :
its
.I jobs
tree, then its
.I transcripts
tree.
.IP 2. 4
The shared trees,
.BR "\-\-sharedroot auto" :
for each tree the first root that holds it,
.I /opt/karvi/shared
else
.IR /var/lib/karvi/shared ,
its
.I jobs
then its
.IR transcripts .
A shared tree the operator cannot write to is reported as skipped.
.IP 3. 4
The scoreboard directory,
.BR \-\-scoreboards .
.PP
As root, a run walks instead every private root under
.I /opt/karvi/users
and then under
.IR /var/lib/karvi/users ,
then the shared trees and the scoreboards as above.
A private root under an operator's home is that operator's own, and a
root run does not look there.
The collection directory is never walked.
Candidates from every tree are removed oldest first.
.SH OUTPUT
One line per item on standard output, the summary last; standard error
carries a usage error, or an error that stops the run, alone.
.PP
.nf
.RS
removed kind=activity path=/opt/karvi/shared/jobs/260817/260817\-153859\-00 age=40d bytes=14151
failed kind=activity path=/opt/karvi/shared/jobs/260817/260817\-153859\-02 error=unlinkat .../summary.json: permission denied
examined=31 removed=15 skipped=4 not_owned=0 failed=1 bytes=137313 dry_run=false
.RE
.fi
.PP
The event words are
.B removed
.RB ( would\-remove
under
.BR \-\-dry\-run ),
.BR failed ,
and, under
.BR \-\-verbose ,
.B kept
with one reason
.RB ( young ,
.BR live ,
.BR not\-owned ,
.BR not\-a\-day\-folder ,
.BR symlink ,
.BR unreadable )
and
.B walk
for every place looked at;
.B skipped
names a tree not walked.
The age is whole days, hours under a day, minutes under an hour; a job's
age counts from its end, an orphan's from the newest thing in it, a day
folder's from its date.
The summary counts the records
.BR examined ,
the items
.B removed
(or that would be), the entries
.B skipped
(a name that is not a day folder, a live record, a tree not walked),
the items another user owns
.RB ( not_owned ),
the removals that
.BR failed ,
and the
.B bytes
removed.
.PP
.B "\-\-format jsonl"
writes the same report as one JSON document per line: the event word
under
.B event
.RB ( summary
for the last line), the fields under the keys the text form prints, the
age as
.B age_days
(a whole number), the counts and
.B dry_run
as numbers and a boolean.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Everything eligible went, or would have under
.BR \-\-dry\-run .
.TP
.B 1
A removal failed or a tree could not be walked; the report says which.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an unknown flag, a positional argument,
.B \-\-days
below one,
.B \-\-minfree
outside 0 to 100, or a
.B \-\-format
that is neither
.B text
nor
.BR jsonl .
The message and the help go to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/karvi/users/USER\fR, \fI/var/lib/karvi/users/USER
An operator's private root, provisioned by the site
.RB ( "sudo karvi setup shared" ).
.TP
.I \(ti/.local/share/karvi
An operator's private root otherwise.
.TP
.I /opt/karvi/shared\fR, \fI/var/lib/karvi/shared
The shared trees,
.I jobs
and
.IR transcripts .
.TP
.I /dev/shm/karvi/scoreboards
The scoreboard directory.
.SH EXAMPLES
What would go, as this operator, then remove it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
karvi\-prune \-\-dry\-run
karvi\-prune
.RE
.fi
.PP
Also why each item stays, and the places looked at:
.PP
.nf
.RS
karvi\-prune \-\-dry\-run \-\-verbose
.RE
.fi
.PP
The site, every operator's, as root:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo karvi\-prune \-\-dry\-run
sudo karvi\-prune
.RE
.fi
.PP
Two weeks' retention, the report to the journal as JSON:
.PP
.nf
.RS
karvi\-prune \-\-days 14 \-\-format jsonl | logger \-t karvi\-prune
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR karvi\-prune.timer ,
the per-operator and the site's systemd timers, and the cron script
.IR karvi\-prune ,
shipped with karvi's packaging;
.I docs/PRUNE.md
(the guide: the reasons and the schedules) and
.I docs/OPERATIONS.md
"Retention" in the karvi source.
